course: dictionary
lesson: 12768
title: Easterly: wind and direction
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Easterly means towards the east, or coming from the east. The word is built from east, and the -ly ending shows it describes a direction or a wind.
explain: «The wind was easterly, so it blew from the east.» An easterly wind is named by where it comes FROM. It blows from the east towards the west, like a breeze at your back if you face west.
explain: «We walked in an easterly direction, towards the sunrise.» Easterly can describe a direction too. Easterly can also be a noun: «The easterlies blew all week» means the easterly winds.
fact: Easterly means towards the east, or coming from the east.
fact: An easterly wind is named by where it comes from: it blows from the east towards the west.
fact: On a map with north at the top, east is on the right, and the sun rises in the east.
fact: «The easterlies» is another name for the trade winds, which blow from the east.
fact: Compass words work in a set: north, south, east and west, with northerly, southerly, easterly and westerly to match.
exercise: «The flag flapped in an easterly wind.» What does easterly mean here? | Very hot and dry | Blowing from the west | *Blowing from the east | Blowing up from the ground
exercise: Which way does an easterly wind blow? | Towards the east, from the west | Towards the north | *Towards the west, from the east | Straight up and down
exercise: Which compass direction does the word easterly come from? | West | South | North | *East
test: «Ships sailed in an easterly direction for many days.» Where were the ships heading? | Towards the west | Towards the north | Towards the south | *Towards the east
test: Mia says, «The easterly is blowing hard.» What is she talking about? | A map of the town | A bird flying south | *The wind blowing from the east | The sea at low tide
exam: Which sentence about an easterly wind is true? | It blows from the west towards the east | *It blows from the east towards the west | It blows straight down from the sky | It never moves at all
